-- and the theorem: the bridge is not two-centred, so it is not the embedding of any molecule of the
-- standard representation. The two-centre carrier cannot hold it — not awkwardly, not by convention, but
-- because hmol-two-centred proves every molecule it can hold has the property the bridge lacks. That is
-- the inorganic and organometallic problem stated as a fact about carriers rather than as a difficulty
-- with an algorithm, and the general carrier above holds the bridge with nothing added.
bridge-not-two-centred : TwoCentred bridge → Empty
bridge-not-two-centred t =
  case t unit dib-b1 dib-b2 dib-h unit unit unit of
    inl q → dib-b1-not-b2 q
    inr s → (case s of
      inl q → dib-b2-not-h q
      inr q → dib-b1-not-h q)
